-- title:
--   Mod 𝔪 Galois representation for weight-two Hecke algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N \ge 1$ an integer and $S$ a set of natural numbers, and let $\mathbb{T} =$ `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. Let $\mathfrak{m} \subseteq \mathbb{T}$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $p$. The assertion is that there exist a finite field $L$, a ring homomorphism $j : \mathbb{T}/\mathfrak{m} \to L$ and a group homomorphism $\rho : \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, where $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the chosen algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$, with the following four properties. First, $\rho$ factors through a finite level: there is an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ with $K/\mathbb{Q}$ finite-dimensional such that $\rho(\sigma) = 1$ for every $\sigma$ fixing $K$ pointwise. Second, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \neq p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\sigma) = j(T_\ell \bmod \mathfrak{m})$. Third, under the same conditions on $\ell$, $A$ and $\sigma$ but with the requirement $\ell \notin S$ dropped, $\det \rho(\sigma) = \ell$ in $L$. Fourth, for such $\ell$ and $A$, $\rho$ is trivial on the image in $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$.
--
--   This is the weight-two case of the existence of the Galois representation attached to a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra, in the form where the coefficients are allowed to lie in an arbitrary finite field receiving $\mathbb{T}/\mathfrak{m}$ rather than in $\mathbb{T}/\mathfrak{m}$ itself; the trace and determinant conditions express the Eichler–Shimura relations modulo $\mathfrak{m}$. It is used to obtain the version with coefficients in the residue field $\mathbb{T}/\mathfrak{m}$ and the version attached to a ring homomorphism out of the weight-two Hecke algebra.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRep_exists_finiteField_galoisRep_trace_eq_heckeT_mod_of_isMaximal_two.lean

